 "headline": [
  "**Rank methods by a within-environment correlation** for selecting the top 10% in each environment: `ridge_pc40_lo` ranks first by the rank correlation and `mlp` by Pearson r. Both correlations can rank methods for this decision (the rank correlation is admissible, Pearson r is protected against calibration), and in the published outcome tests neither consistently selected better material.",
  "**Choose among `ridge_pc40_lo`, `ridge_pc40_hi`, `mlp`, `ens`, `gbm`** on cost or simplicity: at this trial size (1,948 genotype\u2013environment cells per method) they lie within 0.067 of the best on at least one correlation, the smallest gap such a trial resolves (Gaussian lower bound; calibrated panels needed 0.101\u20130.282).",
  "The first two methods are practically identical on the rank correlation (gap below 0.0001).",
  "Ranking by RMSE would pick `ens` instead; RMSE and Pearson r order 25 % of method pairs in opposite directions.",
  "Out of sample (environment split, 200 splits, outcome reliability 0.68), the method each rule picks recovers 59 % (rank correlation), 77 % (Pearson r) and 37 % (RMSE) of the selection gain attainable over an average method."
 ],
